Z||000000||WhackyAss||01-04-2001||04:24 PM||||Hello, 1st post here.  Anyway the background.  I'm messing with a 91 Firebird, 3.1L auto.  I've got a few other fbodies with V8's and bought the V6 as a beater, no one on any of the fbody boards knows anythign about V6's, so I figure someone here might know the answer to my question.  <P>I'm having problems related to the injectors.  I'm using injectors from a 3.4L Z34 engine, and I think they're responsible.  Can anyone tell me the stock flow rates for a 3.1?  What injectors could be used without creating a problem?  Right now it gets HORRIBLE gas mileage, and floods at stoplights.  <P>Thanks for any help you can provide.||||reg||1
